{"availability":"available","full":"d4mr/bother","name":"bother","description":"a free open source toolkit for batch processing images in the browser","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":9,"forks":1,"created":"2024-02-01T09:33:50Z","updated":"2024-02-08T21:10:58Z","license":"CC-BY-4.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://d4mr.github.io/bother","topics":["batch-image-processor","editing-image","image-processing","offline-capable"],"demo":"https://res.cloudinary.com/dr2xlumqw/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/wrlthx1td8bk6f06wrii","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T16:11:31.884Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T16:11:31.884Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T16:11:31.884Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T14:32:52.868Z","stars":9,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-04T16:11:31.884Z","stars":9,"forks":1}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["bother is a free open source toolkit for batch processing images in the browser.","bother was born out of a need to add white borders to images to make them square, but the process was very bothersome.","existing tools didn't allow for batch processing. some others required uploading to servers which introduced unnecessary latency and bottlenecks, especially since browsers today are a more than capable platform for performing these operations locally on the client. tools are ad-ridden, have shoddy ui, usage limits, etc. you get the idea."],"features":["Current bother supports only padding, but slicing is being developed actively.","padding tool allows adding borders to images (supports batch processing) to get them all to the same target aspect ratio.","use cases include adding white borders to images to make them square, eg, for instagram. you can choose to add padding on the non-dominant axis too, see a live preview, and download the images individually or as a zip…","the slicing tools allows extraction of multiple images from within the same image. this goes beyo